WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.261 --> 00:00:24.209
"It will be easy to find someone to help," Ally thought as she walked through Sandville's downtown area.

2
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.051
But Ally didn't spot any 'Help Wanted' signs.

3
00:00:27.591 --> 00:00:29.331
Nor did she pick up any cries for help.

4
00:00:29.932 --> 00:00:32.798
In fact, she saw hardly any humans on the street.

5
00:00:33.338 --> 00:00:35.360
Most of them were zooming by in vehicles.

6
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.803
Finally she spotted a man walking a four-legged animal with fluffy fur.

7
00:00:42.044 --> 00:00:49.169
She tried to read the man's thoughts but could pick up only a few words: "Milk bread dog

8
00:00:49.209 --> 00:00:55.334
biscuits." It didn't sound like a cry for help, but Ally hurried toward him anyway.

9
00:00:55.354 --> 00:01:01.002
"Greetings! I am Allyzooba of Astralia.

10
00:01:01.443 --> 00:01:02.744
Can I be of help to you?"

11
00:01:05.706 --> 00:01:07.908
The man scooped up his animal and backed away.

12
00:01:08.548 --> 00:01:12.912
Then he hurried off, muttering, "Kids these days are so weird!"

13
00:01:17.896 --> 00:01:22.100
A little farther down the street, a woman stepped out of a store and headed to her vehicle.

14
00:01:25.823 --> 00:01:29.597
Ally tried to read her thoughts, but once again the words and images were fuzzy.

15
00:01:30.798 --> 00:01:31.458
Ally sighed.

16
00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.340
Finding a human to help was going to be more challenging than she'd first thought.

17
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.822
Especially since her Astral mind abilities weren't working well on this strange planet.

18
00:01:41.922 --> 00:01:46.324
But as she glimpsed her reflection in a large plate-glass window, something occurred to her.

19
00:01:47.305 --> 00:01:49.225
Her new human hair was long and thick.

20
00:01:49.245 --> 00:01:51.466
"Hey!" she thought.

21
00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:54.888
"Maybe my hair is creating problems."

22
00:01:56.128 --> 00:01:58.409
She tucked her hair behind her ears and listened again.

23
00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.351
This time a voice rang clearly in her head.

24
00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:05.313
"I need help I can't do everything myself."

25
00:02:07.354 --> 00:02:08.315
Ally looked around.

26
00:02:08.975 --> 00:02:11.036
The cry was coming from the building right in front of her!

27
00:02:12.337 --> 00:02:16.339
She held up her meld medallion to read the sign on the window: Ray's Diner.

28
00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.061
She hurried inside.

29
00:02:22.982 --> 00:02:25.604
Unlike Pepe's Diner, this one was almost empty.

30
00:02:26.368 --> 00:02:30.991
Three people in a booth were sipping hot beverages, and a man wearing a blue uniform and badge

31
00:02:31.031 --> 00:02:32.052
was sitting at the counter.

32
00:02:32.072 --> 00:02:35.655
"I bet he's the one in charge," Ally thought.

33
00:02:40.438 --> 00:02:41.939
Are you the commander here?"

34
00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:42.880
she asked.

35
00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:44.921
The man looked up and laughed.

36
00:02:45.541 --> 00:02:48.624
"Me? I'm just a museum security guard.

37
00:02:49.484 --> 00:02:51.265
Ray's the one in charge around here."

38
00:02:52.466 --> 00:02:54.488
He pointed at a man working inside the kitchen.

39
00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:58.821
Ally walked into the kitchen.

40
00:02:58.841 --> 00:03:04.465
"Greetings! I am Allyzooba of Astralia."

41
00:03:05.766 --> 00:03:10.029
But there was so much noise from the grill and fan, the human named Ray didn't even turn

42
00:03:10.069 --> 00:03:16.113
around. "Excuse me."

43
00:03:16.574 --> 00:03:17.775
Ally tapped him on the shoulder.

44
00:03:19.376 --> 00:03:22.018
"I am Allyzooba of Astralia.

45
00:03:22.978 --> 00:03:28.421
I have come to solve your woes, to do good deeds, and to spread great joy."

46
00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.362
"You don't sound like you're from Australia!"

47
00:03:30.802 --> 00:03:32.042
Ray shouted over the noise.

48
00:03:34.163 --> 00:03:36.864
"Not Australia—Astralia!"

49
00:03:37.264 --> 00:03:38.104
Ally shouted back.

50
00:03:38.124 --> 00:03:41.745
"And I have come to do—" "Look, Ally."

51
00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:43.645
Ray wiped his brow.

52
00:03:43.666 --> 00:03:45.346
"Is it a job you want?"

53
00:03:47.087 --> 00:03:47.547
She nodded.

54
00:03:49.867 --> 00:03:51.828
"Well, I'll hire you," Ray said.

55
00:03:52.468 --> 00:03:56.610
"I need help because I can't cook, wash dishes, and wait on customers by myself.

56
00:03:58.331 --> 00:04:01.513
My son usually helps me, but he's busy this summer with soccer camp.

57
00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:03.314
And I'll be honest.

58
00:04:03.874 --> 00:04:04.715
I can't pay you much.

59
00:04:05.355 --> 00:04:06.516
You'll have to work for tips."

60
00:04:07.797 --> 00:04:11.639
"You mean I can help you and get paid—in dollars?"

61
00:04:12.439 --> 00:04:15.021
"It's not a lot, nothing to get excited about."

62
00:04:15.041 --> 00:04:18.022
"Well, I'm really excited!"

63
00:04:18.463 --> 00:04:19.303
Ally exclaimed.

64
00:04:20.024 --> 00:04:22.625
Ray smiled and grabbed an apron from a hook on the wall.

65
00:04:24.025 --> 00:04:26.006
He handed it to Ally, and she put it on.

66
00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.268
Then he went over to pick up a plate with a triple-decker sandwich.

67
00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:35.590
Take this."

68
00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.152
"Thanks!" Ally licked her lips.

69
00:04:39.732 --> 00:04:42.473
She was about to take a bite when Ray shouted, "No!

70
00:04:43.113 --> 00:04:43.854
What are you doing?

71
00:04:44.774 --> 00:04:46.315
That's for Phil at the counter!"

72
00:04:47.315 --> 00:04:49.556
"Oh! This is for a customer to eat!"

73
00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:50.816
Ally realized.

74
00:04:51.617 --> 00:04:53.277
She headed out of the kitchen with the plate.

75
00:04:54.398 --> 00:04:55.818
But on the way out, she tripped.

76
00:04:55.838 --> 00:05:02.721
"Whoa!" The customers gasped as the sandwich slipped back and forth on the plate.

77
00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:08.464
Then, in the nick of time, Ally managed to catch her balance and save the sandwich.

78
00:05:08.484 --> 00:05:13.306
"Hooray!" The customers clapped.

79
00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.768
Ally smiled and took an Astralian bow.

80
00:05:21.276 --> 00:05:24.998
"Some earthlings are friendly, just as the computer said," she thought.

81
00:05:26.578 --> 00:05:31.100
But others, like the waitress at Pepe's and the man with the furry animal, had treated her rather

82
00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:37.923
meanly. "No wonder humans also have a reputation for being dangerous," she thought.

83
00:05:37.943 --> 00:05:40.284
"They're so unpredictable!"

84
00:05:40.864 --> 00:05:44.226
Plus, Earthlings had never made contact with an Astralian before.

85
00:05:45.146 --> 00:05:49.448
So while Ally was here on Earth, she would have to be careful—very careful.
